## 🔎 3. Search for Sysmon Event ID 11

Run:

```powershell
Get-WinEvent -FilterHashtable @{
    LogName = 'Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational'
    Id      = 11
} -MaxEvents 20 |
Select-Object TimeCreated, Id, Message |
Format-List
```

Review the event message for:

- `Image` — process image path
- `ProcessId` — process identifier
- `TargetFilename` — file path
- `CreationUtcTime` — file creation time, when available
- `User` — user associated with the event, when available

Fields vary by event version. Use the actual message to confirm which fields are present.

