## 💼 12. SOC Interview Questions

**Q1. What does Sysmon Event ID 11 record?**

It records file creation activity, including file paths and associated process information, when the activity is covered by the active configuration.

**Q2. Does Event ID 11 detect every file modification?**

No. It is not a complete file-change audit. Its coverage depends on the event definition and configuration.

**Q3. Why investigate files created in temporary directories?**

These paths can be used by legitimate applications and by suspicious activity, so context helps analysts prioritize investigation.

**Q4. How can a SOC analyst identify the process associated with file creation?**

Inspect the event's process fields and correlate the process GUID with Event ID 1 where available.

**Q5. Does an unusual filename prove a file is malicious?**

No. Analysts should evaluate the path, responsible process, file properties and supporting telemetry.

